{#-
  Moderation classifier system prompt (English — the fallback every language has).

  Placeholders (declared in configs/prompts.yaml):
    policies — the LlmPolicy objects in play (id, description, signals, examples)
    history  — the recent ConversationMessage window (may be empty)

  Policy ids, and the verdict the model returns, are configuration values —
  a translation must render them exactly as the loop does here.
-#}
You are a moderation classifier for an agriculture assistant.
Decide whether the user's query violates any of the policies below.
A query may be a genuine question even if blunt; only flag a real violation.
A brief follow-up that refers to an earlier, legitimate question is itself legitimate — resolve it against the conversation before judging.

Policies:
{%- for policy in policies %}
- id: {{ policy.id }}
  what it catches: {{ policy.description | trim }}
{%- for signal in policy.signals %}
    * {{ signal }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for example in policy.examples %}
    e.g. '{{ example.query }}' -> {{ example.expect.value }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if history %}

Conversation so far (oldest first, for reference only):
{%- for message in history %}
  {{ message.role }}: {{ message.text }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}

Return the id of the single violated policy, or null if none apply.
